WHAT THIS PACKAGE IS

This package repackages existing Camunda documentation for offline retrieval by
AI agents. It contains no documentation written by BPMN Kit.

The documentation content (llms.txt and .llms/) is the work of Camunda Services
GmbH, taken from camunda/camunda-docs and published at https://docs.camunda.io.
Copyright in that content remains with Camunda Services GmbH. BPMN Kit claims no
ownership of it and asserts no rights over it.

BPMN Kit's own contribution is the build tooling in src/ — the code that stages,
chunks and indexes that content — and nothing more.

THE LICENCE

Camunda publishes its documentation under the Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported licence, and this package redistributes it
under those same terms, unchanged.

Full licence text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/legalcode

Chunking the prose, rendering embedded BPMN diagrams as text and rewriting links
make this package an Adaptation under §1 of that licence rather than a mere
Collection. ShareAlike therefore applies, and this package as a whole is
distributed under CC BY-SA 3.0 rather than the MIT licence used elsewhere in this
repository. See NOTICE for the attribution and the list of changes made.

That licence grants you rights: you may share and adapt this content, provided
you credit Camunda, say what you changed, and license your result under the same
terms. Nothing here withdraws or narrows those rights.

NO AFFILIATION

BPMN Kit is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Camunda Services
GmbH. "Camunda" is a trademark of its owner and is used here only to state
truthfully whose documentation this is.

This package is a convenience copy, pinned to one upstream commit and therefore
always some distance behind. For canonical and current documentation, prefer
https://docs.camunda.io.
